{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Silly Superstitions"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Breaking a Wishbone"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 17}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe or unusual events through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le17ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Be Supposed to"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> is used to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span>, in past, present or future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + To be + supposed to + verb"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">weren't supposed to </span>make the cranberry sauce. <br/>I <span class =\"strong\">was supposed to</span> cook the turnkey. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "**Pronunciation tip**:<br/>When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Like this:<br/>Be suppose_to"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wasn't supposed to cook the mashed potatoes."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You were supposed to make a wish."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I was supposed to play this year."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wasn't supposed to participate.<br/> <br/>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Conditional Sentences with <span class=\"italic\">If</span> Clause"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The <span class=\"strong\">first conditional </span> with if clauses is used to exchange opinions about possible future outcomes. <br> The <span class=\"strong\">second conditional </span>  is used to exchange opinions about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": " In conditionals, we have two clauses: the if clause and the condition clause. When the if clause is the first part of the sentence, write a comma before the condition clause. <br><br> To say that something is possible, use the <span class=\"strong\">first conditional </span>  (will or will not do something). In that condition, something else may, may not will or will not happen. <br><br>  <span class=\"prelo-letter-page-break\"></span>You use the <span class=\"strong\">second conditional</span> to talk about unreal or hypothetical situations. There is no certainty that it's possible to fulfill the condition."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">If I had a million dollars, I would buy a car.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "  Do you have a million dollars?  No.<br/> Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really.<br/> What would you do if you had a million dollars? Buy a car."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First Conditional:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First Conditional: 2nd Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If I finish work today, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'll come to the dinner tonight.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible that I can go to the dinner tonight, but only if finish working first. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If my mom could only choose one holiday to enjoy for the rest of her life, she would choose Thanksgiving."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I had one wish, I would wish it to be Thanksgiving everyday."}, {"type": "text", "content": " "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second Conditional:<br/>If ... + Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second Conditional: <br/>would + base verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If I had one meal left to eat in my life, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I would choose my mom's Thanksgiving dinner.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It is an impossible situation and can only happen in a hypothetical situation.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "commercial"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "related to \u200bbuying and \u200bselling things"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: For my mom, Halloween has become too commercial."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about Thanksgiving."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to get together"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to gather or assemble"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My mom enjoys it when family and friends get together and share a big meal. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mashed potatoes"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " \u200bpotatoes that have been \u200bboiled and \u200bcrushed until they are \u200bsmooth"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Last year, I was supposed to cook mashed potatoes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob06aud03"}], "