est of her life, she would choose Thanksgiving. My mom enjoys it when the family and friends get together and share a big meal. She loves to cook, which is good, because I don't. Last year, I was supposed to cook mashed potatoes and I was supposed to make the cranberry sauce, two dishes my family loves to eat. However, I made a mess of both dishes so badly that my mom had to recook them. Everything tasted amazing though, as always. If I had one meal left to eat in my life, I would choose my mom's Thanksgiving dinner.", "id": 2, "image": ""}, {"time": "50000", "text": "Now, Thanksgiving has its own superstition and that is the breaking of the wishbone. In my parent's house, the breaking of the wishbone is a family tradition. The rules are simple; each person grabs an end and gives a yank. If you get the bigger piece, your wish will be granted. Participants are always selected by my mother. I was supposed to play this year, but my mother disallowed it. I guess I've had enough good luck recently. Instead, my little cousin won. His wish: \u201cIf I had one wish, I would wish it to be Thanksgiving every day.\u201d\nA perfect wish.", "id": 3, "image": ""}], "video_src": "engenn8le17ob06re2vid02"}}], "id": 2, "template_override": 1, "type": "video", "title": "", "_data": []}], "id": 0}]}